          "text": "Description: On November 4, 2008, at 7:52 PM, a driver observed for 5 to 10 seconds a slow-moving black triangular object with two white lights on two of its vertices. This observation resembles a low-flying plane, but it seems highly unlikely in this location. This observation case is of low strangeness (slowly moving white lights) and low consistency (weather inconsistency and very short observation duration for a moving witness in their vehicle). This case is classified C due to lack of information.",
